  "diagnosis": [
    "The historical graph candidate improves supported exact-route accuracy and latency but worsens near-domain safety, so it is not promotable.",
    "The dominant supported failure mode is false abstention in operation fit, followed by capability fit; wrong-tool errors are rare.",
    "For accepted supported rows, the pairwise operation top choice is usually correct, including 129 of 130 baseline wrong-endpoint cases, but the ordinary operation-fit gate currently does not use that choice to reorder/select.",
    "Near-domain false routes are highly concentrated in semantically adjacent unsupported actions, especially support ticket reopen/priority/escalation requests mapping to support.create_ticket. A scalar relevance threshold alone cannot reliably represent this capability boundary.",
    "The existing graph semantic seed mixes tool-domain, operation-action, endpoint-description, and field terms into one embedding surface and resolves very few requests directly on this corpus. A separated tool-domain then within-tool operation ablation is justified."
  ],
  "next_actions": [
    "Evaluate an opt-in operation-fit selector that uses the already-authorized pairwise top option after the same acceptance gate.",
    "Evaluate the preregistered hierarchical tool-domain then within-tool operation representation.",
    "Add explicit negative/unknown capability evidence for semantically adjacent unsupported actions instead of solving support-family failures only by raising a global threshold.",
    "Keep calibration and blind corpora ungenerated until a development candidate passes all standing gates and is frozen."
  ]
